{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson","id":926975,"title":"Question for Ian Watson","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-06T04:07:32-07:00","id":926975,"title":"Question for Ian Watson","content":"Ian: I read the chapter you wrote on Aberrants for the Trinity Storytellers Handbook. In that chapter, you stated that Daredevils do not wield energy the way Aberrants or psions do, and are in fact nothing more than extremely skilled and/or luckyhumans. However, the preview text I've read clearly implies that Talents are a third type of Inspired and, therefore, more than human. It doesn't matter for purposes of my game--I've already decided that in my campaign Talents are wielders of probability energy--but I am curious to learn the canon answer. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:23:14-07:00","id":928200,"title":"","content":"If anyone other than Ian has any information or opinions, please feel free to chime in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:32:53-07:00","id":928211,"title":"","content":"I didn't write the Aberrant material in the TSH: That was Stew Wilson.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where your confusion lies. There is no disagreement between the statements &quot;Daredevils do not wield a third type of energy the way Aberrants and psions do&quot; and &quot;Daredevils are a kind of Inspired.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:26:31-07:00","id":928238,"title":"","content":"The confusion is this: are Talents merely extremely skilled and/or lucky humans, or are they more than human? I thought all Inspired by their very nature were more than human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:53:04-07:00","id":928263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=928238#post928238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The confusion is this: are Talents merely extremely skilled and/or lucky humans, or are they more than human? I thought all Inspired by their very nature were more than human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me ask you a question: what is luck?<br /> <br /> Many people have written that luck is the unconscious application of extreme or unknown skill. Max Gunthor says &quot;events that influence one's life and are <i>seemingly</i> beyond one's control&quot;, his emphasis not mine. Jung describes synchronicity as events being related without causal relationship.<br /> <br /> So, by extension: why do you assume that luck itself is not a force within the universe? If you can't control your skill, can it be said that it's not possible for someone else to master it? If someone can be verified to have extreme luck, are they more than human? If, as Gunthor notes, this preternatural luck is beyond their control, does it cease to be luck? If, as Jung says, there is a meaningful relationship to be inferred without a causal one, does that make the Inspired somehow superhuman?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:19:08-07:00","id":928288,"title":"","content":"I think what Neall is trying to say is that Talents unconsciously manipulate luck. That is exactly what they do in my game. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:20:20-07:00","id":928332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=928288#post928288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what Neall is trying to say is that Talents unconsciously manipulate luck. That is exactly what they do in my game. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I'm also saying it doesn't make them superhuman, or even more than human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T08:19:13-07:00","id":929747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=928332#post928332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but I'm also saying it doesn't make them superhuman, or even more than human.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How does the manipulation of subatomic or atomic particles to influence the events of a given circumstance to benefit you in a certain way make them human?<br /> Being able to dodge faster...being able to shift a wound so that it is not as critical as it could be...how are these human things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T09:27:38-07:00","id":929787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=929747#post929747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the manipulation of subatomic or atomic particles to influence the events of a given circumstance to benefit you in a certain way make them human?<br /> Being able to dodge faster...being able to shift a wound so that it is not as critical as it could be...how are these human things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Collapsing a waveform is an ability of consciousness, not superhuman ability. Humans already do this all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:21:48-07:00","id":929848,"title":"","content":"I agree with thedonnie. If you can manipulate luck, that's a superpower. It's kind of like coincidental magick in Mage: the Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T21:05:08-07:00","id":930700,"title":"","content":"I can play Chopsticks on the piano. Some people can compose symphonies. Are they superhuman? Or do they just possess more skill than I do?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty good at math, but some people can figure out incredibly complex equations in their head. Are they superhuman? Or do they just possess more talent than I do?<br /> <br /> Some people are lucky. Some people are luckier than others. Are they superhuman?<br /> <br /> There's a reason we call them &quot;Talents.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T08:54:25-07:00","id":930880,"title":"","content":"I think this is basically a semantic discussion. As long as Talents get to roll some dice to simulate their ability (conscious or otherwise) to manipulate luck, I'll be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:00:29-07:00","id":930887,"title":"","content":"I think part of what Neall and Ian are saying is that Talents are &quot;normal&quot; humans who can stand on a relatively equal footing with novas and psiads. I have no problem with this. In fact, in my crossover campaign, I made the archaeologist Jordan Kettridge (from the Vampire Clan Novels) a Talent (technically, I used the Daredevil rules from Adventure! to create him, but I prefer the term Talent). I have no problem with Talents being normal humans who happen to be especially skilled and/or lucky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T12:01:34-07:00","id":930966,"title":"","content":"Unless it is specifically written down that they are only highly skilled humans, then I will cleave to my own idea that they are people who manipulate things on a subatomic level to influence how some things play out. That may even be a houserule. <br /> With that being said, I can accept that Talents can be just incredibly and highly skilled humans. After all, there are numerous examples of things like that. Such as every action movie ever made. Not to mention the killer in any non-supernatural horror movie. Or even the cunning mastermind who plots things out well beforehand such as Batman. I am just saying that I would like to have mine manipulate particles to stick with the way the other two flavors do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T19:54:54-07:00","id":931150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=930966#post930966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless it is specifically written down that they are only highly skilled humans, then I will cleave to my own idea that they are people who manipulate things on a subatomic level to influence how some things play out. That may even be a houserule.<br /> With that being said, I can accept that Talents can be just incredibly and highly skilled humans. After all, there are numerous examples of things like that. Such as every action movie ever made. Not to mention the killer in any non-supernatural horror movie. Or even the cunning mastermind who plots things out well beforehand such as Batman. I am just saying that I would like to have mine manipulate particles to stick with the way the other two flavors do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a great quote about Ethan Hunt in the last Mission Impossible, &quot;Sir, Ethan Hunt is the living manifestation of destiny.&quot; While it's lazy having a derivative of &quot;manifest&quot; in such close proximity to &quot;destiny,&quot; it is how I feel Talents/Daredevils can likely be described. I don't know if this indicates that they're consciously manipulating sub-quantum particles or some such Dancing Wu Li gobbledegook but it does feel like the archetype for the character classification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T09:45:19-07:00","id":931416,"title":"","content":"You can argue that Talents aren't superhumans with some semantic shenanigans but at the end of the day they get narrative superpowers, really, and that's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T19:34:38-07:00","id":931763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=931416#post931416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can argue that Talents aren't superhumans with some semantic shenanigans but at the end of the day they get narrative superpowers, really, and that's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's Aberrant's thematic playground, not core Trinity's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T04:27:51-07:00","id":931919,"title":"","content":"But what about Project Tantalus, the sub-division of Project Utopia set up to study paramorphs? If paramorphs/Daredevils/Talents are just exceptionally skilled and/or lucky human, then what's to study? Alternatively, if Maxwell Mercer is the only paramorph in the setting, there's not much for Project Tantalus to study there either. Please explain. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T06:45:54-07:00","id":931966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=931763#post931763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's Aberrant's thematic playground, not core Trinity's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aberrant is about characters with actual superpowers, not narrative ones though. By narrative superpowers I mean granted a degree of mechanical superiority by virtue of being significant to the narrative.<br /> <br /> In the setting, they don't have superpowers. In the game, they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T10:01:39-07:00","id":932067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=931416#post931416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can argue that Talents aren't superhumans with some semantic shenanigans but at the end of the day they get narrative superpowers, really, and that's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it! At this point the characters in Fast-Furious don't have particular super powers but they do seem to have narrative ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T11:21:09-07:00","id":932112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Anne Country</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=932067#post932067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it! At this point the characters in Fast-Furious don't have particular super powers but they do seem to have narrative ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a fine way to look at it.<br /> <br /> There <i>are </i>some in-game shenanigans in terms of deducible alteration of probability (Doctor Primoris even comments on this in Adventure! and Continuum follows the same theme), but like Ian said it's an emergent property of humanity's place within the Continuum and not a sharp divide between human and superhuman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T13:48:59-07:00","id":932621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=931919#post931919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about Project Tantalus, the sub-division of Project Utopia set up to study paramorphs? If paramorphs/Daredevils/Talents are just exceptionally skilled and/or lucky human, then what's to study? Alternatively, if Maxwell Mercer is the only paramorph in the setting, there's not much for Project Tantalus to study there either. Please explain. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting question, isn't it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's almost like Aeon's asking the same questions a lot of people in this thread are asking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T14:02:54-07:00","id":932628,"title":"","content":"Essentially humans in the setting have some sort of weird probability effecting capability which seems to work off certain mind/skill sets, scenarios and events, is what I am getting. They aren't superhumans in the sense that it is an element of humanity that they have such potential capability, however they are in the sense that we, in real life, don't have that same tangible ability to affect probability. There seems to be no demarcation between those who can do it and those who don't, rather it is a spectrum that everyone is on (but most people are so low that they might as well have fallen off the bottom).<br /> <br /> Not that any of this really affects me since I am an Aberrant guy and Aberrant alone, but it's my understanding.<br /> <br /> When are these games coming out, anyway? Seems like I've heard nothing for ages...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T06:59:47-07:00","id":932887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/926975-question-for-ian-watson?p=932628#post932628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When are these games coming out, anyway? Seems like I've heard nothing for ages...</div> </div> </div> </div>After Scion!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T18:14:23-07:00","id":934223,"title":"","content":"They did state that August would be the KS for Scion. I would hope that it is not that long after that they have the Trinity KS...at which point, I will look like the most popular Fry meme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:48:46-08:00","id":1056309,"title":"","content":"In short, if we're positing a setting in which certain people can develop the potential to control quantum energies with their minds, it's not to much of a longshot to suggest that even ordinary people interact with the fundamental forces of the universe in extremely subtle ways that are indistinguishable from happenstance, yet that some of those seemingly ordinary people are a bit more &quot;keyed in&quot; than others, so that those forces just seem to line up for them even when they don't consciously do anything to cause it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"htt